    "wikipedia_summary": "<i><b>Bupleurum lancifolium</b></i> is a species of flowering plant in the family Apiaceae known by the common name <b>lanceleaf thorow-wax</b>. It is native to the Mediterranean Basin and it is known elsewhere, including parts of North America, as an introduced species. It grows up to 50 centimetres (20 in) tall with a hairless, waxy stem around which leaves are fused at their bases. The dull, waxy, deep-green leaves are narrowly lance-shaped to nearly oval and 3 to 10...",
